@model bool
@*
    The race dock's strip: the course elevation profile, with the field's speed traced over it — the
    median inside a p10–p90 band, on the profile's own chainage axis. Those were two stacked canvases
    until the pair became one picture ("where the course climbs, the field slows"), which is not
    readable across two charts you have to line up by eye.

    Section boundaries are placed HERE and never on the map: this course passes the Mt Baker ski area seven
    times, so one map pixel is seven different chainages. The field rides the profile too — same positions,
    same colours, same filter as the map.

    The model is one bool: whether the viewer may edit. It only changes the profile's aria-label —
    click-to-place is gated in race-replay-view (editable:false on the share fork).
*@
<div class="race-profile-wrap">
    <canvas id="raceProfile" class="race-profile"
            aria-label="@(Model ? "Course elevation profile with field speed — click to split a section" : "Course elevation profile with field speed")"></canvas>
</div>
